        },
        {
          "name": "Tree Node B",
          "type": "InNodeType&"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Bool",
      "docs": "determine whether two nodes occupy the same space in their trees\nfor example if you have a tree key/value pairs, AreMatching should compare the keys while AreValuesEqual\nshould compare the values\n@param TreeNodeA node from the first user provided tree (guaranteed not to be null)\n@param TreeNodeB node from the second user provided tree (guaranteed not to be null)\n@param OutDifferingProperties optional output list of property paths for the properties that differs between the two nodes"
    },
